ess><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUKA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANJI YOSHIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANDA, SATORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUKA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANJI, YOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HANDA SATORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUKA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANJI YOSHIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANDA, SATORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUKA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANJI, YOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Conventionally, the level of the electromagnetic wave radiated from the resonance state of an electrical resonance structure is about one hundredth of the transmission level of a calling radio wave of a sensor, the level is further lowered when demodulated information codes are superimposed by installing an IC to an electrical resonance structure, and hence sufficient directivity and detection distance are not realized.  To solve the problem, according to the invention, an annular coil for causing electric resonance in response to a first frequency and a capacitor are housed in a closed case made of a nonmagnetic material so as to prevent change in quality.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Traditionnellement, le niveau de l'onde électromagnétique émise par rayonnement d'une structure de résonance électrique à l'état rayonnant est égal à environ un centième du niveau de transmission d'une onde radio d'appel d'un capteur, ce niveau est encore abaissé lorsque des codes d'informations démodulés sont superposés par l'installation d'un circuit intégré sur la structure de résonance électrique et une directivité et une distance de détections suffisantes ne sont par conséquent pas obtenues. Pour résoudre ce problème, selon cette invention, une bobine annulaire servant à produire une résonance électrique en réponse à une première fréquence et un condensateur (1) sont logés dans un boîtier fermé fabriqué en un matériau non magnétique, afin d'empêcher les variations de qualité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>